DTSTAMP:20260804T195451Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:[Maine Agencies] MaineCare Telehealth Services Provider Licensure 
 Requirements
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			MaineCare Telehealth Services Provider Licensure Requir
 ements\nMaineCare Telehealth Services Provider Licensure Requirements\nAug
  04\, 2026\nAs a reminder\, all providers delivering telehealth services t
 o MaineCare members must be enrolled with MaineCare and must comply with M
 aineCare Benefits Manual\n(MBM) Chapter I\, Section 4: Telehealth Services
 \n.\nChapter I\, Section 4 requires that providers be “\nappropriately l
 icensed\, accredited\, certified\, and/or registered in the state where th
 e member is located during the provision of the telehealth service.\n”\n
 This means that all providers delivering in-person or telehealth services 
 to MaineCare members\, who are in Maine at the time of the service\, must 
 hold appropriate Maine credentials or Interstate Licensure Compacts recogn
 ized by the\nDepartment of Professional and Financial Regulation\n(DPFR) o
 r other appropriate organization.\nPursuant to\nMBM\, Ch. I\, Section 1.18
 \nfailure to comply with these requirements can result in the denial of cl
 aims or recoupment of payment because services delivered without proper st
 ate licensure are not eligible for reimbursement.\nFor questions\, please 
 contact your\nProvider Relations Specialist\n.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs
 /oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-telehealth-services-provider-l
 icensure-requirements-2026-08-04
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-
 telehealth-services-provider-licensure-requirements-2026-08-04
CATEGORIES:Maine Agencies
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4c824fbd45f2175f@agency-mainecare-bulletins.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260804T195451Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:[Maine Agencies] Upcoming Pause in Configuration Changes
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Upcoming Pause in Configuration Changes\nUpcoming Pause
  in Configuration Changes\nAug 04\, 2026\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, 
 the Office of MaineCare Services is launching an upgraded MIHMS\, our clai
 ms processing system\, in October 2026. To support system readiness activi
 ties\, MaineCare is temporarily pausing the implementation of configuratio
 n changes from the end of August to the end of October.\nCoding and NDC Re
 quests\nContinue submitting coding requests to\nOMS.referencefile@maine.go
 v\nand NDC/J-Code Requests to\nMaineCareNDCrequest.DHHS@maine.gov\n. Reque
 sts submitted by August 19\, 2026\, if approved\, will be implemented no l
 ater than the last synchronization on August 25\, 2026. Continue to submit
  these requests as usual after these dates. MaineCare will review and docu
 ment change requests beginning at the end of October.\nRate Change Request
 s\nContinue submitting rate change requests as usual to\nMIHMSRateRqst.DHH
 S@maine.gov\nthroughout this period. MaineCare will review and document ch
 ange requests as appropriate for implementation beginning at the end of Oc
 tober.\nClaims and Billing Inquiries\nContinue directing claims and billin
 g inquiries to Provider Services at 1-866-690-5585. We will continue revie
 wing claim denials to determine if a configuration change is needed. Maine
 Care will review and document change requests as appropriate for implement
 ation before the configuration pause or beginning at the end of October.\n
 We appreciate your continued cooperation during this transition. If you ha
 ve questions about the configuration pause or the status of a request\, pl
 ease contact\nyou\nr\nProvider Relations Specialist\n.\nhttps://www.maine.
 gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/upcoming-pause-configuration-cha
 nges-2026-08-04
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/upcoming-p
 ause-configuration-changes-2026-08-04
CATEGORIES:Maine Agencies
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ffd4305c3d7fd634@agency-mainecare-bulletins.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260803T151311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
SUMMARY:[Maine Agencies] Provider Responsibility Regarding Third Party Lia
 bility and Secondary Billing
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Provider Responsibility Regarding Third Party Liability
  and Secondary Billing\nProvider Responsibility Regarding Third Party Liab
 ility and Secondary Billing\nAug 03\, 2026\nIn a previous\nnotice\n\, the 
 Office of MaineCare Services (OMS) reminded providers of your responsibili
 ties regarding third -party liability and secondary billing. Pursuant to M
 aineCare Benefits Manual (MBM) Ch. I Section 1.07-3(B)\, MaineCare is the 
 payor of last resort. OMS announced that we will update the billing and cl
 aims system requirements to accurately reflect the provider’s obligation
  to bill primary insurance when other coverage is available.\nEffective Au
 gust 10\, 2026\, our claims system will no longer treat most Current Proce
 dural Terminology (CPT) and Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System (HCP
 CS) codes as exempt from billing the primary commercial carrier. In accord
 ance with MBM Ch. I Section 1.07: Third Party Liability\, providers must s
 eek payment from the primary carrier before billing MaineCare for all clai
 ms for these services for members with primary coverage\, even when:\nthe 
 billing codes for same services vary between payors\; and\nthe primary pay
 or’s service coverage applies only to a portion of the MaineCare defined
  service. For example\, this applies when the MaineCare service is more co
 mprehensive than the primary payor’s coverage.\nMaineCare also recognize
 s that many provider types that were previously unable to enroll in Medica
 re can now enroll and bill Medicare as the primary payor for services deli
 vered to members dually eligible for Medicare and Medicaid. Providers elig
 ible to enroll with Medicare to deliver Medicare reimbursable services mus
 t do so to receive MaineCare reimbursement as a secondary payor.\nMaineCar
 e’s claims system will accept an Explanation of Benefits (EOB) with prim
 ary dollars attached even if the billing codes differ. The sys\nhttps://ww
 w.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/provider-responsibility-
 regarding-third-party-liability-and-secondary-billing-2026-08-03
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/provider-r
 esponsibility-regarding-third-party-liability-and-secondary-billing-2026-0
 8-03
CATEGORIES:Maine Agencies
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:97237996b1a4f300@agency-mainecare-bulletins.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260803T151311Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
SUMMARY:[Maine Agencies] Attention Trading Partners: Take Action Now Befor
 e MaineCare’s New Online Portal Goes Live
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: Take Action Now Before Main
 eCare’s New Online Portal Goes Live\nAttention Trading Partners: Take Ac
 tion Now Before MaineCare’s New Online Portal Goes Live\nAug 03\, 2026\n
 A refreshed and upgraded MIHMS is coming in mid October 2026. The Office o
 f MaineCare Services (OMS)\, in partnership with Gainwell Technologies\, i
 s launching an upgraded MIHMS\, to bring enhanced security\, improved usab
 ility\, and a more modern experience to better support your day-to-day wor
 k.\nThe upgrade will include a new “MaineCare Partner Portal” that wil
 l replace what is known today as the “Health PAS Online Portal.” Pleas
 e note that\, until the October go-live\, we will continue using the name 
 “Health PAS Online Portal” in communications related to current functi
 onality.\nYou can read more about the benefits to providers and members on
  the\nHealth PAS Online Portal\n.\nTrading Partners Preparation\nThis mess
 age is part of a series about changes to how trading partners will access 
 the new portal and what you must do now to prepare for these changes.\nTra
 ding partners include providers\, billing agents\, health plans\, clearing
 houses\, and business associates. Trading partners have an important role 
 to play in supporting a smooth transition and uninterrupted access to the 
 portal after go-live.\nPortal Access Impacts and Required Actions Before G
 o‑Live\nThe preparation activities and changes below will improve system
  security by ensuring the right people have the right access\, at go-live 
 and ongoing. Most actions are only for Admin (R7) users.\nMost important:\
 nProviders with duplicate emails need to make changes to their portal user
  accounts\nnow\nto assist with account migration to the upgraded portal.\n
 On September 1\, we will terminate current Admin (R7) user accounts that s
 hare an email address with another user account.\nWe will not terminate Ad
 min (R7) us\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/a
 ttention-trading-partners-take-action-now-mainecares-new-online-portal-goe
 s-live-2026-08
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-take-action-now-mainecares-new-online-portal-goes-live-20
 26-08
CATEGORIES:Maine Agencies
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
